{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And of Naftali he said: Naftali, sated with favor.</b> Jacob blessed him with the blessing of 'a hind let loose, that gives comely words' — for his fruits ripen quickly, and therefore they bring first-fruits from his land before all others. This is what it says: 'that gives comely words' — for in the bringing of first-fruits they praise and give thanks to HaShem. Therefore it is said here, that he is 'sated with favor' — for HaShem sated him with every desire, and therefore he is 'full of the blessing of HaShem,' for he blesses HaShem first, through the bringing of first-fruits. For in the place where Jacob said 'that gives comely words,' here it says 'and full of the blessing of HaShem.' 'The sea and the south shall he possess' — that he has a portion in the sea of Kinneret and in the south."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:16:42.548748996Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}